Z||000005||sqoach||12-04-2001||02:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Uaana:<BR><B>Sounds like a cool idea. hmm what number is the blue one? 4?? I think putting a metal sleeve in sounds like a better idea though. Lot easier to reglue the sleeve the reattach a stripped ball.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Nope, that would be the 2 ball. The 4 is purple. That might be kinda neat, because I'm thinking of doing my interior trimmed in blue. Those pool balls are kinda big, though.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>                <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigsqoach2.gif"> <BR><B>86 SE V6 - daily driver</B><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 Sport Coupe 2.5L 5spd (soon to be sold)</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ferrari_cdn||12-04-2001||02:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sqoach:<BR><B> Those pool balls are kinda big, though.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Some balls are big, but some are not.  I've played in a local pool club, and I've played in a pool table in a curling club.  The pool club and that pool in the curling club had different sized balls.  So far I've only seen 2 different sizes, the smaller one would be a good size.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ICEFierosig.gif"> AIM: CanadianFiero||||reg||7
